course: dictionary
lesson: 9829
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and swell is one of them. Context tells you which meaning to choose. «They trap the gas, so the dough swells.» Here swell means to get bigger and puffier, because the gas fills the dough.
explain: Now look at a different meaning: «Big waves mean a big swell, so listen to the lifeguards.» A swell is the long, smooth rise and fall of waves in the sea. The word waves and the lifeguards tell you it is about the sea.
explain: Some clues come from feelings. Swell can also mean a feeling growing strong inside you, as in «a swell of pride». Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Swell can be a verb, a noun, or an adjective, depending on how it is used.
fact: «Swell» means to get bigger, rounder or fuller, often because of injury, water or air.
fact: «Swell» can also mean to grow in number, size, loudness or strength, as in «The crowd swelled».
fact: A swell is the long, smooth rise and fall of waves in the sea.
fact: Old-fashioned American slang uses «swell» to mean excellent, as in «That's swell!»
exercise: «They trap the gas, so the dough swells.» What does swells mean here? | *Gets bigger and puffier | Makes a loud noise | Turns into water | Goes flat and hard
exercise: «Big waves mean a big swell, so listen to the lifeguards.» What is a swell? | A red flag on the beach | A loud shout from the sea | *The long, smooth rise and fall of waves | A sore, painful ankle
exercise: Dad says, «That's swell!» What does swell mean here? | Painful and sore | Sad and quiet | Big and wet | *Excellent, very nice
test: «The crowd swelled as the match went on.» What does swelled mean here? | Fell quietly | Went to sleep | Turned into water | *Grew in number and loudness
test: «She felt a swell of pride when her name was called.» What does swell mean here? | Got smaller | Went numb | Went red in the face | *A feeling growing strong inside
exam: Which sentence uses swell as a noun meaning big waves? | A bee sting made my hand swell | Her heart would swell with joy | *The big ocean swell pushed the boats towards the shore | We swelled the crowd with cheers
